{{!
    @template tool_lp/module_navigation

    Filter a course's competencies by an activity, overridden by Dimensions.

    Mirrors tool_lp/module_navigation of Moodle 5.3 (2026100500), admin/tool/lp/templates/module_navigation.mustache.
    Re-diff it against that file on every core upgrade.

    Kept from core, because tool_lp/module_navigation and core/form-autocomplete read them: the select's
    id module-nav-<uniqid> (the JavaScript below binds and enhances it by that id), its label, the
    form's class user-competency-course-navigation (tool_lp's stylesheet hides the native select under
    it; the autocomplete draws its own control in its place), the hidden fields courseid and mod, every
    option with its value and selected state, and the JavaScript itself. The module names keep core's
    double stash.
    Changed: the panel is the theme's (dim-comp-nav) in place of core's bordered box; core's float
    stays, because the page beneath was laid out around it.
    The JavaScript is core's statement for statement, with the constructor's parameter capitalised
    (Nav) and long lines wrapped: core's copy has no example context and was never linted.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * courseid, moduleid, baseurl - read by the JavaScript
    * hasmodules - boolean
    * modules - array of id, selected, name

    Example context (json):
    {
        "courseid": 2,
        "moduleid": 0,
        "baseurl": "https://example.com/admin/tool/lp/coursecompetencies.php",
        "hasmodules": true,
        "modules": [
            {"id": 0, "name": "All activities", "selected": true},
            {"id": 5, "name": "Case study", "selected": false}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="dim-comp-nav float-end">
<form class="user-competency-course-navigation">
<input type="hidden" name="courseid" value="{{courseid}}">
<input type="hidden" name="mod" value="{{moduleid}}">
{{#hasmodules}}
<span class="dim-comp-nav__group">
<label for="module-nav-{{uniqid}}" class="accesshide">{{#str}}filterbyactivity, tool_lp{{/str}}</label>
<select id="module-nav-{{uniqid}}">
{{#modules}}
<option value="{{id}}" {{#selected}}selected="selected"{{/selected}}>{{name}}</option>
{{/modules}}
</select>
</span>
{{/hasmodules}}
</form>
</div>
{{#js}}
require(['core/form-autocomplete', 'tool_lp/module_navigation'], function(autocomplete, Nav) {
    (new Nav('#module-nav-{{uniqid}}', '{{baseurl}}', {{courseid}}, {{moduleid}}));
{{#hasmodules}}
    autocomplete.enhance('#module-nav-{{uniqid}}', false, false, {{# quote }}{{# str }}filterbyactivity, tool_lp{{/ str }}{{/ quote }});
{{/hasmodules}}
});
{{/js}}
